if DAC_PCM512X

    config PCM512X_MAX_VOLUME
        int "Maximum DAC volume (dB)"
        range -100 0
        default 0
        help
            Maximum volume level in dB that corresponds to AirPlay volume 0 dB.
            The usable P0-R61/R62 range is 0 dB to -103 dB; the boost half of
            the register (up to +24 dB) is deliberately not used.

            Unlike the TAS57xx, a PCM512x drives a 2.1 Vrms line output rather
            than a speaker, so the default is 0 dB — full scale. Lower it if
            the amplifier downstream clips before the volume control reaches
            the top of its range.

    config PCM512X_ANALOG_GAIN_MINUS_6DB
        bool "Attenuate the line output by 6 dB"
        default n
        help
            Set P1-R2 LAGN/RAGN, dropping full scale from 2.1 Vrms to about
            1.05 Vrms. Useful when feeding an input that expects a 1 Vrms
            consumer line level. This is analogue attenuation, so it costs no
            resolution — prefer it over PCM512X_MAX_VOLUME for a fixed offset.

    config PCM512X_FORCE_BCK_PLL
        bool "Always derive the PLL from BCK"
        default n
        help
            By default the driver puts the PLL on MCLK when it detects one on
            the SCK pin, and falls back to BCK otherwise. Set this to keep the
            PLL on BCK even when MCLK is present.

            Only useful for testing the no-MCLK path on a board that has one.

endif
